-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/905dd765-bb1a-48f4-b866-f0576a53ba2c
-- title:
--   Theorem 5 — star-convex functions with a globally non-degenerate optimal set
-- statement:
--   Let $F\subseteq\mathbb R^n$ be a closed convex set, let $f$ be twice differentiable on $F$ with gradient $f'(x)$ and Hessian $f''(x)$, and let $x_0\in\operatorname{int}F$ be such that the level set $\mathcal L(f(x_0))=\{x: f(x)\le f(x_0)\}$ lies in $\operatorname{int}F$. Assume the Hessian is $L$-Lipschitz on $F$ in the spectral norm, $L>0$ (Assumption 1). Fix $0<L_0\le L$ and let $x_0,x_1,\dots$ be generated by method (3.3): at step $k$ a parameter $M_k\in[L_0,2L]$ is chosen, $x_{k+1}=T_{M_k}(x_k)$ is a global minimizer of the cubic model $\langle f'(x_k),y-x_k\rangle+\frac12\langle f''(x_k)(y-x_k),y-x_k\rangle+\frac{M_k}6\|y-x_k\|^3$, and the acceptance test $f(x_{k+1})\le\bar f_{M_k}(x_k)$ holds.
--
--   Assume $f$ is star-convex (Definition 1) and its optimal set $X^*$ is globally non-degenerate with constant $\gamma>0$ (Definition 2). Let $x^*\in X^*$, $\Delta_k=f(x_k)-f(x^*)$ and
--   $$\bar\omega=\frac1{L^2}\Big(\frac\gamma2\Big)^3 .$$
--   1. If $\Delta_0\ge\frac49\bar\omega$, then during the first phase of the process
--   $$f(x_k)-f(x^*)\le\Big[(f(x_0)-f(x^*))^{1/4}-\frac k6\sqrt{\frac23}\,\bar\omega^{1/4}\Big]^4 .\qquad(4.4)$$
--   The phase ends at the first index $k_0\ge0$ with $\Delta_{k_0}\le\frac49\bar\omega$, and such an index exists ($k_0=0$ if already $\Delta_0\le\frac49\bar\omega$); (4.4) holds for all $k\le k_0$.
--   2. For $k\ge k_0$ the sequence converges superlinearly:
--   $$f(x_{k+1})-f(x^*)\le\frac12\,(f(x_k)-f(x^*))\sqrt{\frac{f(x_k)-f(x^*)}{\bar\omega}} .\qquad(4.5)$$
--   Quadratic growth of the whole optimal set replaces non-degeneracy of the Hessian, so the result covers minimizers lying on connected manifolds.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: f twice differentiable on F → gradient g and Hessian H given by HasGradientWithinAt f (g x) F x and HasFDerivWithinAt g (H x) F x at every x ∈ F; reason: derivatives are relative to F, so no smoothness of the ambient extensions outside F is required; the source derivatives imply these, and on int F they are the ordinary derivatives
--   - encoding: iterates x_0, x_1, … and T_{M_k}(x_k) any global minimizer → 0-based sequence x with the published run predicate IsCubicNewtonRun (any global minimizer, acceptance test as f(x_{k+1}) ≤ f(x_k) + model value); reason: the minimum of the model is attained at x_{k+1}, so this is f̄_{M_k}(x_k); same runs
--   - reading: (4.4) 'at the first phase'; 'This phase is terminated as soon as f(x_{k0}) − f(x*) ≤ (4/9)ω̄ for some k0 ≥ 0' → there is a first index k₀ with Δ_{k₀} ≤ (4/9)ω̄ (Δ_j > (4/9)ω̄ for j < k₀); (4.4) for every k ≤ k₀ when Δ₀ ≥ (4/9)ω̄; (4.5) for every k ≥ k₀; reason: the first phase consists of the indices before termination; at k₀ itself the bound follows from the same step
--   - encoding: f(x*) for x* ∈ X*; ω̄ → f xs for an arbitrary global minimizer xs; a variable ω with ω = (1/L²)(γ/2)³; reason: all minimizers have the same value; same constant
-- source:
--   Nesterov & Polyak, Cubic regularization of Newton method and its global performance, Math. Program. Ser. A 108 (2006) 177–205, DOI 10.1007/s10107-006-0706-8, p. 190, Theorem 5, (4.4)–(4.5)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CubicNewton_Shared_IsCubicNewtonRun
import Definitions.Def_CubicNewton_StarConvex_IsStarConvexFn
import Definitions.Def_CubicNewton_Nonconvex_Supplement_IsGloballyNondegenerate

namespace CubicNewton.Nonconvex.Supplement

/-- Nesterov–Polyak 2006, Theorem 5, p. 190, with `ω̄ = (1/L²)(γ/2)³`. Standing assumptions of
Section 2, Assumption 1, a run of method (3.3) with `0 < L₀ ≤ L`; `f` is star-convex
(Definition 1) and its optimal set is globally non-degenerate with constant `γ` (Definition 2);
`xs` is a global minimizer. Writing `Δ_k = f(x_k) − f(x*)`, there is a first index `k₀` with
`Δ_{k₀} ≤ (4/9) ω̄` (end of the first phase; `k₀ = 0` when already `Δ₀ ≤ (4/9) ω̄`);
if `Δ₀ ≥ (4/9) ω̄`, then (4.4) holds for every `k ≤ k₀`; and (4.5) holds for every `k ≥ k₀`. -/
theorem theorem_5 {n : ℕ}
    (F : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ)
    (g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (H : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) →L[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (L : ℝ)
    (hF_closed : IsClosed F) (hF_convex : Convex ℝ F)
    (hf : ∀ x ∈ F, HasGradientWithinAt f (g x) F x) (hg : ∀ x ∈ F, HasFDerivWithinAt g (H x) F x)
    (hL : 0 < L) (hLip : ∀ x ∈ F, ∀ y ∈ F, ‖H x - H y‖ ≤ L * ‖x - y‖)
    (x₀ : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hx₀ : x₀ ∈ interior F)
    (hlevel : {x | f x ≤ f x₀} ⊆ interior F)
    (L₀ : ℝ) (hL₀ : 0 < L₀) (hL₀L : L₀ ≤ L)
    (x : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (M : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hrun : CubicNewton.Shared.IsCubicNewtonRun f g H L₀ L x₀ x M)
    (hstar : CubicNewton.StarConvex.IsStarConvexFn F f)
    (γ : ℝ) (hnd : IsGloballyNondegenerate F f γ)
    (ω : ℝ) (hω : ω = 1 / L ^ 2 * (γ / 2) ^ 3)
    (xs : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hxs : ∀ y, f xs ≤ f y) :
    ∃ k₀ : ℕ, f (x k₀) - f xs ≤ 4 / 9 * ω ∧ (∀ j < k₀, 4 / 9 * ω < f (x j) - f xs) ∧
      (4 / 9 * ω ≤ f x₀ - f xs →
        ∀ k ≤ k₀, f (x k) - f xs ≤
          ((f x₀ - f xs) ^ (1 / 4 : ℝ) - (k : ℝ) / 6 * Real.sqrt (2 / 3) * ω ^ (1 / 4 : ℝ)) ^ 4) ∧
      ∀ k ≥ k₀, f (x (k + 1)) - f xs ≤
        1 / 2 * (f (x k) - f xs) * Real.sqrt ((f (x k) - f xs) / ω) := by sorry

end CubicNewton.Nonconvex.Supplement
